<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:33:23Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Skyscraper in Riyadh damaged as Saudi Arabia reports surge in new Houthi attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bace047e2e31ab21a7f083cdcfcd44c71d1e990afe9fa117365a73a49e8ba0b4</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:33:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T07:58:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261119-skyscraper-in-riyadh-damaged-as-saudi-arabia-reports-surge-in-new-houthi-attacks--e54170cb555f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261119-skyscraper-in-riyadh-damaged-as-saudi-arabia-reports-surge-in-new-houthi-attacks" /><summary type="html">A skyscraper in Saudi Arabia's capital Riyadh was damaged on Thursday after the Gulf country reported new attacks by Yemen's Houthis. Witnesses said the city's Public Investment Fund Tower, which showcases Saudi Arabia's economic ambitions, was "damaged across several floors, with windows blown out".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Gaza: Israel launched new offensive on Nuseirat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74a7cb8d7d01258b56357012e355690c2f5255d0bfc0b4c1220586c3cafc468d</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:33:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T07:50:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/gaza-israel-launched-new-offensive-on-nuseirat--5e7b3fc17c6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/gaza-israel-launched-new-offensive-on-nuseirat" /><summary type="html">Israeli tanks have moved east of the Nuseirat refugee camp in central Gaza, with witnesses reporting heavy shelling, gunfire and airstrikes as the Israeli military says it has launched an operation in a Hamas-controlled area. Strikes killed at least three people on Wednesday, and displaced families are fleeing again, saying there is no real ceasefire. Israel and Hamas accuse each other of breaking the truce in force since October 2025, while Gadi Eisenkot tries to form a government after inconclusive elections.</summary></entry><entry><title>Middle East crisis poses 'largest threat' to energy security in history, warns IEA</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f37b134f6ed50aeb61c174f741f7359c158f2d49b1401b040772374aaed547b7</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T05:11:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261119-middle-east-crisis-energy-security-iea--bef2931d058a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261119-middle-east-crisis-energy-security-iea" /><summary type="html">The International Energy Agency said on Thursday that the Middle East crisis triggered by US and Israeli strikes on Iran in February posed the “largest threat” to energy security in history. It warned that consumers were bearing more of the costs as Iran’s blockade of the Strait of Hormuz disrupted oil shipments.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli army launches ground operation in Hamas-controlled area of Gaza</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e72aefc9b5ae04acb72f3f4dabcf0c623b6623d5ff1c32953cb36892e12c016f</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T19:55:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israeli-army-launches-ground-operation-in-hamas-controlled-area-of-gaza--842ad9ad2dc7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-army-launches-ground-operation-in-hamas-controlled-area-of-gaza" /><summary type="html">The Israeli military said it had launched an operation on Wednesday in a Hamas-controlled area of central Gaza, where an AFP journalist saw Israeli tanks position themselves east of the Nuseirat refugee camp. The rare ground operation comes after inconclusive Israeli elections, with the opposition's Gadi Eisenkot trying to form a government without caretaker prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu, who has built his brand on saying he will ensure Israel's security. FRANCE 24's Daniel Whittington reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Writer Etgar Keret: 'The Israel my parents dreamed of' is still possible, but not under Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e92beeb93ce25375ea819e2f8a631cad86456f8cbe641a9bf12b66fc0809d54</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T19:45:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261118-netanyahu-s-only-2-tickets-are-racism-or-starting-a-war-he-stopped-acting-as-a-democratic-p--f0085602677a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261118-netanyahu-s-only-2-tickets-are-racism-or-starting-a-war-he-stopped-acting-as-a-democratic-player" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Israeli writer and filmmaker Etgar Keret, author of "The Seven Good Years". Keret argues that Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu is seeking to remain in power, at any cost, including delegitimising Arab parties and prolonging conflict. "For him, it could be a never-ending war as long as he's in power. He has no incentive to stop it," our guest warns.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Gazans flee shelters as Israeli army launches ground operation beyond Yellow Line</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e18dc44f5f1f086cfca3efe062761e4085e000c66a904539faae48649c42acf1</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T16:03:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-gazans-flee-shelters-as-israeli-army-launches-ground-operation-beyond-yellow-line--9caf8473edb4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-gazans-flee-shelters-as-israeli-army-launches-ground-operation-beyond-yellow-line" /><summary type="html">Palestinians fled their tents and shelters in central Gaza on Wednesday after Israel launched a rare ground operation in an area it withdrew ​from under a ‌2025 ceasefire. The Israeli army said it crossed the Yellow Line separating Israeli and Hamas-controlled areas "to remove a threat posed to IDF troops operating in the Gaza Strip".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Why the Houthis may besiege Aden rather than storm it</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6dcf1cd78408be115fe9eadedd427c7f9ba6a14f48b3a50b909137874c589c19</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:55:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-yemen-why-the-houthis-may-besiege-aden-rather-than-storm-it--cc45be20d135.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-yemen-why-the-houthis-may-besiege-aden-rather-than-storm-it" /><summary type="html">Bolstered by their recent military successes, Houthi rebels this week advanced close to the southern port city of Aden, the interim capital of the internationally recognised Yemeni government. Amid territorial ambitions, regional rivalries, and divisions within government forces, the potential fall of this stronghold could permanently alter the balance of power in the country.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Loud blast rocks Riyadh as Saudi-led coalition says it intercepted Houthi missiles</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae9b7462fa358c0f1db3ef5c9b6e7998fe51239caef8387ab8abf55f05fb2aa5</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T02:06:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-middle-east-live-kuwait-bahrain-report-drone-and-missile-attacks--e3338d2d36dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-middle-east-live-kuwait-bahrain-report-drone-and-missile-attacks" /><summary type="html">A powerful explosion rattled homes in Riyadh on Wednesday, journalists and residents said, as the Saudi-led coalition fighting Yemen's Houthis said they intercepted two cruise missiles fired by the Iran-backed militia. In Gaza, the Israeli military launched a rare ground operation in a Hamas-controlled area, leading dozens of families to flee their tents and shelters. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli parliament elects Eisenkot ally Matan Kahana as speaker in blow for Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d8ee0aa1aa177f0515d5713c1d4861b66d2d3c1c597d815a721442f5e03b305</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T21:24:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261117-_-israeli-parliament-elects-eisenkot-ally-matan-kahana-as-speaker--0f0856a90608.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261117-%F0%9F%94%B4-israeli-parliament-elects-eisenkot-ally-matan-kahana-as-speaker" /><summary type="html">The Israeli parliament on Tuesday elected as new speaker an ally of Gadi Eisenkot, the party leader currently working to form the next government and replace current Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Matan Kahana, a former special forces soldier, is expected as soon as Wednesday to start the process of undoing much of the agenda of Netanyahu.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Major setbacks for Netanyahu ahead of vote to name new Knesset speaker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c414e1cde99c881fc3306c59254daf9c056723f741f1ee8d5a6edf81349500ce</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T21:05:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/major-setbacks-for-netanyahu-ahead-of-vote-to-name-new-knesset-speaker--42690b87e83b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/major-setbacks-for-netanyahu-ahead-of-vote-to-name-new-knesset-speaker" /><summary type="html">Since suffering heavy losses in Israel’s Oct. 27 election, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's party has repeatedly claimed the vote was “stolen” by Arab-led parties, possibly with foreign assistance. Those claims appear to be crumbling as he tries to cling to power, as the Israeli parliament is set to select a new speaker opposed to him. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.</summary></entry><entry><title>Did the US use ‘blackout bombs’ in Iran? Images reveal mysterious fibres at infrastructure sites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2231bc5c001a88c681edb9dd328eaa8ca2b31078f2763755861130d68e18c361</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T14:39:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261117-iran-us-graphite-blackout-bombs-infrastructure--975fba07e48f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261117-iran-us-graphite-blackout-bombs-infrastructure" /><summary type="html">Photographs published by Iranian local media suggest that US forces may have used graphite bombs, also known as ‘blackout bombs’, against infrastructure in Iran in recent days. These weapons are designed to disrupt electricity supplies by causing short circuits rather than physically destroying power facilities.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Breaking taboos: Egypt's sexual revolution takes to social media</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:021ebce04cf186a57d48a29d3d19c28ff9cef39466c9ba84ac70b1843a597c26</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T09:50:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261116-breaking-taboos-egypt-s-sexual-revolution-takes-to-social-media--b6d3a1224ba6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261116-breaking-taboos-egypt-s-sexual-revolution-takes-to-social-media" /><summary type="html">In Egypt, a sexual revolution is quietly unfolding on social media. Accounts followed by tens of thousands of people, with posts attracting millions of views, are tackling a wide range of issues surrounding sexuality – from the widespread practice of female genital mutilation (which 93 per cent of women in rural areas have undergone) to sex education and sexual pleasure.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Eisenkot says Netanyahu ‘cannot remain’ after alleged election interference by aide</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f1c6162a2b889c755e8c5fea3051d51160753e2330b5c8cb3a9d4ac373280ff</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T03:47:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261116-eisenkot-netanyahu-cannot-stay-in-office--9f48760f0aa3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261116-eisenkot-netanyahu-cannot-stay-in-office" /><summary type="html">Israeli prime ministerial hopeful Gadi Eisenkot said on Sunday caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu must leave office immediately following reports of alleged electoral interference by a Netanyahu aide. The former army chief called Netanyahu and his entourage an "immediate threat to democracy", hours after representatives discussed forming a national unity government.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Houthis advance on Aden as government forces retreat to defend their capital</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:219fc71ce5bc6f3fe5dad4ff63af1136be0c1171f9afa27ccc6208b777357aea</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T19:28:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-yemen-houthis-advance-to-within-60-kilometres-of-aden-military-sources-say--21793fe41f25.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-yemen-houthis-advance-to-within-60-kilometres-of-aden-military-sources-say" /><summary type="html">Houthi forces in Yemen have advanced to within 60 kilometres of Aden, the seat of the country's internationally recognised government, military and government sources said Sunday. The embattled government earlier announced it was pulling back its last forces from the Bab el-Mandeb Strait to defend its temporary capital on the southern coast of Yemen.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel kills senior member of Hamas's military wing in Gaza strike</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:698cd773a5ca101bdefd74582d5a9018d9bc698142d9e0bc1d67957dca436702</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T16:41:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-israel-kills-senior-member-of-hamas-s-military-wing-in-gaza-strike--b280762ad201.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-israel-kills-senior-member-of-hamas-s-military-wing-in-gaza-strike" /><summary type="html">The Israeli military said on Sunday its forces had killed a senior member of Hamas's military wing in Gaza. The militant group confirmed the death of Samir Abu Younis, the commander of its Rafah brigade, adding that he played a prominent role in planning the October 7, 2023 attacks.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran claims drone attack on US military base in Bahrain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8380e3424fcca563a0e0a36ace18c654f9254579b4a586d121a1d044c87f506</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T15:29:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-claims-drone-attack-on-us-military-base-in-bahrain--f851a46df3dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-claims-drone-attack-on-us-military-base-in-bahrain" /><summary type="html">Bahrain issued two alerts of potential threats on Sunday, its first such warnings since September as blasts rocked the capital, Manama. It comes after Iran targeted an airbase in the US-allied island state, ending a long lull in strikes during the Middle East War and comes as negotiations to end the conflict remain at a stalemate, with the US maintaining its naval blockade and Iran its stranglehold over the strait of Hormuz. Story by Rachael Griffiths.</summary></entry><entry><title>Bahrain says air defences destroyed several Iranian drones attacking US base</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd03afd34214af732cf53b1d6e25ea39e3970609eb2fed5d0aa5f1866771c652</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T13:55:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/bahrain-says-air-defences-destroyed-several-iranian-drones-attacking-us-base--e8fd9186a781.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/bahrain-says-air-defences-destroyed-several-iranian-drones-attacking-us-base" /><summary type="html">Bahrain issued two alerts of potential threats on Sunday, its first such warnings since September. The second Iranian drone attack in three days, ending a long lull in strikes during the Middle East war. Diplomatic efforts to end the almost nine-month conflict have yet to produce a breakthrough, with ​sporadic attacks continuing. Details from the ground by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Tehran, Reza Sayah.</summary></entry><entry><title>Global diesel prices ease as winter approaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0424a59c03e1c7a0605218adef30ccaad20d332fae57946f2176c18998dcb060</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T10:40:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/global-diesel-prices-ease-as-winter-approaches--8c37061055b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/global-diesel-prices-ease-as-winter-approaches" /><summary type="html">Global diesel prices, which have remained elevated since the start of the Iran war and the blockade of the Strait of Hormuz, have fallen sharply in recent weeks as Gulf exports recover and global oil supplies get back on track for the first time since February. The price drop is being felt in Europe, where prices remain roughly 77% above pre-war levels, and in the US, where the national average fell below $6 a gallon on Saturday. Details by Liza Kaminov.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran claims drone attack on US military airbase in Bahrain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:775962d8a2251c211138f1a55306a91b3b7075bfd2d8c436e359fea1967e1580</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T09:57:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-iran-claims-attack-on-us-military-airbase-in-bahrain--23e345aee6b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-iran-claims-attack-on-us-military-airbase-in-bahrain" /><summary type="html">Iranian military confirmed on Sunday an attack on a US military base in Bahrain, in its second targeting the Middle Eastern country in the space of three days. Bahrain's military said it had intercepted several Iranian attacks, with the foreign ministry confirming its air defence systems had shot down Iranian drones, preventing them from reaching their intended targets.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Three sentenced to death over Jordan church attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2db83aeaee009de3d0c4f049b981fc492eefef6480bd36854ae036abc09d5c59</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T08:53:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-three-sentenced-to-death-over-jordan-church-attack--cfdbddd0326e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-three-sentenced-to-death-over-jordan-church-attack" /><summary type="html">A Jordanian court on Sunday sentenced the three gunmen responsible for a terror attack on a church funeral procession in the village of Hamoud that killed nine and wounded others. The attack prompted retaliatory strikes on "terrorist organisations" in neighbouring Syria.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu renews call for Israeli unity government as Eisenkot dismisses 'tricks'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae321278da0ac1b52db53d47bbb05daa50dc12ac7e9f0747c427329c2df2fa68</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T20:35:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261114-netanyahu-renews-call-for-israeli-government-unity-as-eisenkot-dismisses-tricks--fd54d0cd7431.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261114-netanyahu-renews-call-for-israeli-government-unity-as-eisenkot-dismisses-tricks" /><summary type="html">Israeli caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Saturday renewed his call for a national unity government with Gadi Eisenkot, who dismissed the appeal as a political ploy. This comes as the incoming premier is in the midst of negotiations to form a new administration.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey and Qatar pledge unified stance against attacks in mutual defence pact</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:062a4a9049f4ca77f39b0f0df18b4b14f48ef14ccd64cf173d3790fa8df98dca</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T20:06:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261113-turkey-and-qatar-pledge-unified-stance-against-attacks-in-mutual-defence-pact--78a12542999d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261113-turkey-and-qatar-pledge-unified-stance-against-attacks-in-mutual-defence-pact" /><summary type="html">Turkey and Qatar signed a mutual defence agreement Friday, pledging a unified response to any attack on either country, the two leaders said in a joint statement. The defence pact follows the Mecca Joint Defence Agreement signed by Turkey, Pakistan and Saudi Arabia in August.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>West Bank: ‘Without international trade and financial support, large settlements would not exist’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:232fa22a6cf4f3097d282ca67c1b86723de6fe28262e93a133a7e0ff877b33e8</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:15:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-west-bank-without-international-trade-and-financial-support-large-settlements-would-not-exi--ca01d4fe66ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-west-bank-without-international-trade-and-financial-support-large-settlements-would-not-exist-1" /><summary type="html">France is considering legislation to restrict trade with Israeli settlements in the occupied Palestinian territories, namely the West Bank. Ivar Ekeland, Professor Emeritus at Paris Dauphine-PSL University and Chair of the Organization of Academics for the Respect of International Law in Palestine, discusses the proposed measures with Alison Sargent. He calls for restrictions to cover n ot only goods but also services, including financial services, insurance and tourism. "Without the support of financial entities, of insurance, of providing goods and so on, settlements, big settlements, would not exist," he argues.</summary></entry><entry><title>UN refugee chief Barham Salih slams 'shameful' war in Sudan, urges 'political solution'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7095d458afcbd4a9cd61b0b9aea0025055d066ac68689038416cc7b292ceb3c8</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:56:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261113-un-refugee-chief-barham-salih-slams-shameful-war-in-sudan-urges-political-solution--a499e7d27829.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261113-un-refugee-chief-barham-salih-slams-shameful-war-in-sudan-urges-political-solution" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, UN refugee chief Barham Salih called the war in Sudan "shameful" and urged the world to end it. With forced displacement at a record high, he warned that funding cuts are hurting people "in dire need". "Efficiency has its limits," he said. Salih also defended the "integrity of the asylum system".</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>The truth about Douma: How Syria covered up a chemical attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd3aaef116fc07c6a81f5429dd3e0d12af275f612f5162ca1be39a5ee589e5d6</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T14:24:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261113-the-truth-about-douma-how-syria-covered-up-a-chemical-attack--8968af757dd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261113-the-truth-about-douma-how-syria-covered-up-a-chemical-attack" /><summary type="html">On April 7, 2018, the Syrian town of Douma, on the outskirts of the capital Damascus, was targeted by a chemical attack. Evidence pointed to the Syrian regime, yet proof vanished, and eyewitnesses went silent. Eight years later, FRANCE 24's Jenna Le Bras tracked down survivors and witnesses of the deadly attack. She also met representatives of some of the world's most powerful institutions to understand how a massive cover-up campaign had been orchestrated by the regime, with Russian support.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>'No war, no peace' situation between US and Iran 'cannot continue', Iraqi FM says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76744742bf144bab2119046a90ff5253cfd30acce32343e8391d4a5824f335e5</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T10:28:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261113-no-war-and-no-peace-between-the-us-and-iran-cannot-continue-iraqi-fm-says--e67d72355ae2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261113-no-war-and-no-peace-between-the-us-and-iran-cannot-continue-iraqi-fm-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, Iraqi Foreign Minister Fuad Hussein said the "no war and no peace" situation in the region "cannot continue". He also said that closing all but two border crossings with Iran, as Washington demands, was "not possible". Finally, he confirmed that Iraqi oil now is now flowing through the Strait of Hormuz under US protection.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli strike on Gaza hospital kills six, including surgeon, medics say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32d1e8161b51eb5ab8b87cd2b5ded762d5b7101b3c266f7f1f09b311149f752d</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T20:03:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israeli-strike-on-gaza-hospital-kills-six-including-surgeon-medics-say--1b011ef48705.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-strike-on-gaza-hospital-kills-six-including-surgeon-medics-say" /><summary type="html">Israeli fire killed 11 people in Gaza on Thursday, six of them in the bombing of Nasser hospital in south Gaza early in the day, health officials said, the deadliest single strike since Israel's elections last month. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Dr Goher Rahbour, a surgeon working at the Nasser Hospital.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel to ban far-left French politician Jean-Luc Mélenchon from entry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95c735da71891b3ead958107292e5a37d25c021ee5b1a3cdfc97db47400cac12</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T17:43:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261112-israel-to-ban-far-left-french-politician-jean-luc-m_lenchon-from-entry--505a56d1442f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261112-israel-to-ban-far-left-french-politician-jean-luc-m%C3%A9lenchon-from-entry" /><summary type="html">The Israeli government said Thursday that it would ban far-left French leader Jean-Luc Mélenchon from entering the country after the French presidential contender said he would use French vessels to force aid into Gaza if he were elected. The announcement comes a day after France confirmed it had refused entry to the head of a body representing settlements in the occupied West Bank.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel kills six in Gaza hospital strike as 9-month-old baby freezes to death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bafc67b848336648b7ed3a9db876d1ca9d6bd9da78f97684dd3a8eec222ddfb4</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:18:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261112-israel-kills-six-in-gaza-hospital-strike-as-9-month-old-baby-freezes-to-death--43c83484c699.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261112-israel-kills-six-in-gaza-hospital-strike-as-9-month-old-baby-freezes-to-death" /><summary type="html">An overnight Israeli air strike on Nasser Hospital in southern Gaza killed at least six Palestinians Thursday, including a teenage boy and a surgeon, medics said. Elsewhere in the devastated Palestinian territory, a nine-month-old baby died from the cold as families flee worsening flooding.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>How FRANCE 24 traced Tehran-backed Afghan fighters from Syria to southeastern Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7399c2d12f6f642e10df902dd0562beb9d17fb633d5423ddce8e7cd4f66099c0</id><updated>2026-11-20T07:31:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:03:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261112-iran-afghan-fatemiyoun-fighters-syria-baluchistan--13c8bcd20e3a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261112-iran-afghan-fatemiyoun-fighters-syria-baluchistan" /><summary type="html">Members of the Tehran-backed Afghan Shia militia known as the Fatemiyoun division have resurfaced in Iran after largely disappearing from public view following the fall of Bashar al-Assad’s government in Syria in 2024. FRANCE 24 used "martyrdom” announcements and the geolocation of videos shared on social media to trace their presence.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry></feed>
